What about this?

```
var a = 2;
var x = a >= (true ? 2 : 3);
```

@alberto Your example isn't limited to ternary, though. Any (every?) "concise body" arrow function can be confusing in one way or another, no?

``` js
var a = 2;
var x = a >= (true ? 2 : 3);
var y = a >= (b || a);
var z = a >= Math.sin(a);
```

Isn't this static typing jurisdiction?
